mixin () {
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    "## FarmPath Backend\n\nA per-user farm tracking backend for pepper growers. The crop catalog and its lessons are global reference data seeded at install time; every logged activity and lesson completion is owned by the principal that created it, and callers only ever see their own farm data.\n\n### Authentication and authorization\n\nEvery farm endpoint requires a signed-in, registered caller. Two distinct failures are possible:\n\n- An **anonymous** caller is rejected by the endpoint's own guard with the trap message `Unauthorized: Only users can perform this action`.\n- A **signed-in but unregistered** caller is rejected by the authorization layer with the trap message `User is not registered`.\n\nRegistration happens only when a caller signs in through the app's own frontend (the Internet Identity flow calls `_initialize_access_control`). The first principal to register becomes `#admin`; every subsequent principal becomes `#user`. A direct API caller must therefore sign in through the app once before any farm call succeeds. A principal derived against a different Internet Identity derivation origin is a different principal than the one the frontend registered, so it is treated as unregistered even if it belongs to the app owner.\n\nThe frontend pins an Internet Identity derivation origin, published at `/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin` when available. An agent already holding the user's Internet Identity authorization derives the correct per-app principal against that origin (for example `icp identity link web <name> --app <host>`). Such a delegation acts with the user's full authority in this app until it expires.\n\nAll farm endpoints are available to both `#admin` and `#user` roles; there is no admin-only farm operation. Ownership is enforced per record: activities and lesson completions are keyed by the caller's principal, and operations on another principal's record return `null` (or `false` for delete) rather than trapping.\n\n### Units and encodings\n\n- `CropId`, `LessonId`, and `ActivityId` are `Nat`s, assigned sequentially from 0. The seeded catalog uses crop ids 0-2 and lesson ids 0-9; user-added crops continue from the next free id.\n- `Timestamp` is an `Int` in nanoseconds since the Unix epoch (`Time.now()`).\n- `date` is a UTC day index: whole days since the Unix epoch (`timestamp / 86_400_000_000_000`).\n- `ActivityKind` is a variant: `#harvest`, `#sale`, or `#cost`.\n- `quantity` is a `Nat` in the activity's `unit` (e.g. \"kg\", \"crate\"); `amount` is a `Nat` in the smallest currency unit (0 for harvests).\n- `note` is optional (`?Text`).\n- `profit` is an `Int` and may be negative; `income` and `cost` are `Nat`s.\n\n### Methods\n\n- `listCrops() : [CropView]` (query) - the crop catalog, each with `lessonCount` and the caller's `completedCount`, sorted by crop id.\n- `getCrop(id) : ?CropDetail` (query) - one crop plus its lessons ordered by `order`, each flagged `completed` for the caller. Returns `null` when the crop does not exist.\n- `completeLesson(lessonId) : ?CropView` (update) - marks a lesson complete for the caller. Idempotent: a second call leaves the existing completion unchanged. Returns `null` when the lesson does not exist.\n- `uncompleteLesson(lessonId) : ?CropView` (update) - removes the caller's completion. Safe to call when no completion exists. Returns `null` when the lesson does not exist.\n- `progressSummary() : ProgressSummary` (query) - total and completed lesson counts plus per-crop progress.\n- `addCrop(input) : CropView` (update) - adds a crop to the catalog and returns its view with zero lessons and zero completions.\n- `listActivities(cropFilter, kindFilter) : [ActivityView]` (query) - the caller's activities, newest first (by id descending), optionally filtered by crop id and/or kind. Pass `null` for no filter.\n- `logActivity(input) : ActivityView` (update) - logs a harvest, sale, or cost for the caller.\n- `updateActivity(id, input) : ?ActivityView` (update) - edits an owned activity. Returns `null` when the activity does not exist or is not owned by the caller.\n- `deleteActivity(id) : Bool` (update) - deletes an owned activity. Returns `false` when the activity does not exist or is not owned by the caller.\n- `profitSummary() : ProfitSummary` (query) - total income, total cost, total profit, and a per-crop breakdown. Only `#sale` activities count as income and only `#cost` activities count as cost; `#harvest` contributes to neither.\n- `dashboardSummary() : DashboardSummary` (query) - active crop count (crops with at least one lesson), upcoming task count (currently always 0), the five most recent activities, and `hasData` (false when the caller has no crops and no activities).\n- `getApiDoc() : Text` (query) - this document.\n\n### Lifecycle and polling\n\nProgress and profit figures are derived at read time from stored activities and completions, so a query always reflects the latest writes. `date` is a UTC day index; clients should re-query after UTC midnight rather than caching day-relative values across days. There are no background jobs or asynchronous state transitions: every update completes within its own call.\n\n### Mutation retry safety\n\n`completeLesson` and `uncompleteLesson` are idempotent, so retrying a failed call is safe. `logActivity` and `addCrop` are not idempotent: each successful call allocates a new id and creates a distinct record, so a retried call can produce a duplicate. `deleteActivity` is idempotent in effect (a second call returns `false`). `updateActivity` overwrites the record with the supplied input, so retrying it is safe.\n\n### Errors and limits\n\nAuthorization failures trap: anonymous callers with `Unauthorized: Only users can perform this action`, unregistered signed-in callers with `User is not registered`. Operations on a record the caller does not own return `null` (or `false` for delete) rather than trapping. There is no pagination; list endpoints return every matching record the caller owns. The crop catalog is shared across all callers, so `addCrop` adds a crop visible to everyone.";
  };
};
